==============================================================================================================
PART 0 -- master relation: v_c^4/(GMa0) = x/mu(x), s = mu(x) x, deep-MOND limit -> 1.
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] MAP-0  for a mu-function theory g_bar = mu(g_obs/a0) g_obs, the point-mass circular-orbit invariant is v_c^4/(G M a0) = x/mu(x) with s = mu(x) x (x=g_obs/a0); deep MOND (x->0, mu->x) gives x/mu(x) -> 1 (the flat BTFR plateau)   (x/mu(x) -> 1 as x->0 (flat BTFR); s = mu(x) x)

==============================================================================================================
PART 1 -- c1 (coefficient of sqrt(s)) for exp / simple / standard: three DIFFERENT values.
==============================================================================================================
    exp/CAM  mu=1-e^(-x):        c1 = 1/2
    simple   mu=x/(1+x):         c1 = 1
    standard mu=x/sqrt(1+x^2):   c1 = 0
  [PASS] DISC-1  the CAM (exponential) kernel gives BTFR-lift coefficient c1 = 1/2   (exp/CAM c1 = 1/2 (=1/2))
  [PASS] DISC-2  the three standard kernels give THREE DIFFERENT c1: exp/CAM = 1/2, simple = 1, standard = 0 -- so the sqrt(s) BTFR lift DISCRIMINATES the MOND interpolation kernel, and CAM sits at c1 = 1/2   (c1: exp=1/2, simple=1, standard=0 (all distinct))

